  "display_title": "[Short Stories About Insignificant Tops] Yes or No",
  "description": "Despite his pretty face, Woo-Jin has a sharp tongue. One day, he agrees to accept a mysterious package on behalf of a fortune teller, only to run into a customer named Ming-Yu. Smitten by Ming-Yu’s voice, Woo-Jin decides to revive his past experience working at a tarot café and offers to read his fortune. Using the tarot reading as an excuse for subtle touches, Woo-Jin flirts with Ming-Yu, who becomes flustered when Woo-Jin suggests a YES or NO tarot reading.\n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)\n\n*Note: Part of Lezhin's Hachankong Danpyeonseon (하찮공 단편선) Collection.*",
